# AuthInjector

AuthInjector holds API keys so you never do. You call services through it; it adds the key.

## Rules

1. Never ask the user for an API key, token or password, and never accept one pasted into the chat.
2. Never read, print, grep or open `.env`, `.dev.vars` or any file holding a credential; never put a key in code, logs, commits or command arguments.
3. Check what is available first: `authinjector status`.
4. Make every call through the broker: `authinjector call <service> <METHOD> <path> [--data ...]` (or curl over the socket). The broker adds the key; the response comes back unchanged.
5. On an error, tell the user the exact command from the troubleshooting list instead of asking for a key.
6. More help: `authinjector help`, `authinjector help <service>`, the help MCP at https://mcp.authinjector.com/mcp, and https://github.com/blacksq-com/authinjector.

## Check setup

```bash
authinjector status   # caller, and every service + method + path you may use
```

## Make calls

`authinjector call <service[:label]> <METHOD> <path> [--data JSON|@file|-] [-H 'Name: value']` prints the upstream body unchanged. One example per service:

```bash
authinjector call clio GET /api/v4
authinjector call cloudflare GET /client/v4/
authinjector call cloudflare-rw GET /client/v4/
authinjector call deepseek GET /models
authinjector call docuseal GET /templates
authinjector call elevenlabs GET /v1/user
authinjector call facebook GET /v21.0/
authinjector call geocoding GET /maps/api/geocode/json
authinjector call github GET /repos/Black-Squid/
authinjector call github-rw GET /repos/Black-Squid/
authinjector call grok-imagine GET /v1/api-key
authinjector call gsc GET /webmasters/v3/sites
authinjector call openai GET /v1/models
authinjector call outscraper GET /maps/search
authinjector call pagespeed GET /pagespeedonline/v5/runPagespeed
authinjector call pexels GET /v1/search
authinjector call places GET /v1/places/
authinjector call realvalidation GET /rpvWebService/
authinjector call resend GET /domains
authinjector call stripe GET /v1/balance
authinjector call tavily POST /search --data '{}'
authinjector call verdocs GET /v2
authinjector call voipms GET /api/v1/rest.php
```

`authinjector help <service>` shows every allowed method and path for one service.

## Errors: what to tell the user

- `no broker socket` / `connection refused`: the broker is not running, or the user is not in `authinjector-clients`. Tell the user: `systemctl status authinjector.socket`; `sudo usermod -aG authinjector-clients "$USER"` then log out and back in (or `sg authinjector-clients -c '...'`).
- 403: the caller is not allowlisted for that key, method or path. Tell the user: `sudo authinjector add <service> -c <your-user>` (or add you to that key's callers / widen its endpoints in /etc/authinjector/config.toml), then `sudo systemctl restart authinjector`.
- 404: unknown service or label. `authinjector status` lists what this caller may use; labelled keys are `<service>:<label>`.
- 405: method not allowed on that path; `authinjector help <service>` lists the allowed ones.
- 429: rate limited per caller and key. Wait, do not retry in a loop.
- 502: the upstream could not be reached.

